### Z4 — 2.8 stays closed
No expand / splice probes this pass. `s28_macro_secret_smoke.oo`
integration **exit 0** (sibling `s29_integration.oot`). This audit
does **not** relitigate `macro_expand` / `ast_macro` / import concat.
`${tok}` (13) is a **literal** `oo_str_lit("${tok}")` — 5.8 residual,
not a 2.8 hide.

### Z5 — emit-c compile rail
On every Z1 + Z2 emit-c fail case the C stream contains
`ERR\tsecret\t… sink refuses SECRET …` and rc=1. 06 emits
`oo_print_int((n));` **then** refuses — public first arg only; SECRET
`tok` is never an `oo_print_*` operand.

Runtime `oo_print_str` is unsealed `fwrite`. The **compiler** is the
seal. emit-c still holds it.


